CITATION
--------

If permission has been granted and this software contributes to published
work, please cite MMForge along with the methods it implements:

  Compain, E., Poirier, S., Drevillon, B. "General and self-consistent
  method for the calibration of polarization modulators, polarimeters,
  and Mueller-matrix ellipsometers." Applied Optics 38, 3490-3502 (1999).

  Rosales, A. et al. "Extended eigenvalue calibration method for
  overdetermined Mueller matrix polarimeters." Optics Letters 49,
  1165-1168 (2024).

  Lu, S.-Y., Chipman, R. A. "Interpretation of Mueller matrices based on
  polar decomposition." Journal of the Optical Society of America A 13,
  1106-1113 (1996).

  Gil, J. J., Ossikovski, R. "Polarized Light and the Mueller Matrix
  Approach", 2nd ed. CRC Press (2022).


DISCLAIMER
----------

The Eigenvalue Calibration Method imposes specific requirements on the
instrument. This release targets the custom-built Mueller matrix
spectroscopic ellipsometer at the Department of Optics, Palacky
University Olomouc, and may produce incorrect results on instruments of
a different design without modification.

